;
; How Kitling files one memory of a talk with the companion, in MYRA
; (kitling_rules.h KR5): its number, when it was (ms since 1970), the
; companion's feeling then (swarm_emotion.h palette index) and its
; intensity (0 .. 5), and the tokens the answer cost. Kitling asks whether
; the numbers fit before it keeps them.
^ZXKITLING(seq:i9) = stamp:i15! ^ emotion:i1! ^ intensity:i1! ^ tokens:i9!
